# Pinned opam repository commits, consumed by
# .github/actions/setup-hazel-toolchain.
#
# hazel.opam.locked pins which *versions* the solver picks. It cannot pin their
# *metadata*: opam has no content hashes, and upstream routinely edits
# already-published versions in place rather than cutting new ones. In June 2026
# an in-place edit to conf-libssl.4 / conf-libffi.2.0.0 / conf-zlib.1 broke CI on
# every branch simultaneously with no change on our side (issue #2334). Freezing
# the repository commit closes that hole; the lock file keeps closing the other
# one, and keeps local `make deps` reproducible against the default repo.
#
# Bumped by .github/workflows/update_deps.yml alongside the regenerated lock
# file, so upstream churn can only ever go red inside the bot-update-deps PR.
#
# OPAM_REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE_SHA goes away with issue #1707, which drops our
# dependency on the archive repository entirely.
OPAM_REPOSITORY_SHA=9c0fb80b783c632ef0024ba0cc86df4ced6c19aa
OPAM_REPOSITORY_ARCHIVE_SHA=92f1a8075c3493fa8f4482b885993a91dceee07b
